WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:05.603
Ally and Mateo stepped away from the food truck.

2
00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:08.319
"What's going on?" Mateo asked.

3
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.010
"A lot!" Ally whispered.

4
00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:14.789
"First of all, my powers aren't working."

5
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.950
"Maybe you're just upset because—"

6
00:00:16.951 --> 00:00:20.234
"Ahh!" Just then someone at the truck yelped.

7
00:00:20.235 --> 00:00:23.534
"That sounds like Barry!" Mateo said.

8
00:00:23.535 --> 00:00:26.061
They rushed back to the truck.

9
00:00:26.062 --> 00:00:29.894
"What happened?" Ally asked breathlessly.

10
00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:34.056
"Did you get burned? Are you all right?"

11
00:00:34.057 --> 00:00:37.708
" I'm fine." Barry looked

12
00:00:37.709 --> 00:00:40.743
upset. "But the stove isn't

13
00:00:40.744 --> 00:00:44.899
working." "Let's check the power line," Mateo

14
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.500
said. They went around to the back of Rolling

15
00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:53.195
Ray's. "Look." Mateo pointed to two lines connected to the

16
00:00:53.196 --> 00:00:55.947
truck. "The power line was

17
00:00:55.948 --> 00:00:58.653
cut! So was the propane

18
00:00:58.654 --> 00:01:03.463
line." Barry gasped. "Who would do

19
00:01:03.464 --> 00:01:08.684
that?" "Someone who wants to stop you from entering the contest," Julius

20
00:01:08.685 --> 00:01:13.237
said. "How come you know so much about it?" Barry scowled at

21
00:01:13.238 --> 00:01:15.748
Julius. "Are you the

22
00:01:15.749 --> 00:01:18.127
mole?" "Of course not! I would

23
00:01:18.128 --> 00:01:21.489
never—" Julius began to protest, but Ally jumped

24
00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:27.566
in. "It's not Julius, Barry. But I'm afraid it's another friend of

25
00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:31.403
ours." "Who?" Mateo and Barry asked at the same

26
00:01:31.404 --> 00:01:37.371
time. Ally gulped.

27
00:01:37.372 --> 00:01:40.112
"Flo." "No way!" Barry said.

28
00:01:40.113 --> 00:01:42.940
"It's true," Julius said.

29
00:01:42.941 --> 00:01:47.818
Mateo ran a hand through his hair. "Do you have proof?"

30
00:01:47.819 --> 00:01:51.768
"Julius and I followed her today," Ally said.

31
00:01:51.769 --> 00:01:57.265
"And guess where she went—Pepe's!"

32
00:01:57.266 --> 00:02:02.690
Mateo gasped. "Why did she go there?"

33
00:02:02.691 --> 00:02:06.883
"There's only one reason that I can think of," Ally said.

34
00:02:06.884 --> 00:02:11.928
"To tell them about our plans." She sighed.

35
00:02:11.929 --> 00:02:15.596
"It makes me really sad."

36
00:02:15.597 --> 00:02:20.095
"Well, it makes me mad!" Barry growled.

37
00:02:20.096 --> 00:02:22.495
"I'm going straight to Pepe's to confront them.

38
00:02:22.496 --> 00:02:24.671
They can't steal our recipes!

39
00:02:24.672 --> 00:02:28.689
And then I'm going to text Ray, so he can fire Flo immediately!"

40
00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.129
Mateo formed a T with his hands.

41
00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:37.292
"Time out, Barry. We need solid proof first."

42
00:02:37.293 --> 00:02:42.619
Barry paced around. "Okay, fine."

43
00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:44.656
He looked at Julius.

44
00:02:44.657 --> 00:02:48.331
"Sorry for accusing you without proof."

45
00:02:48.332 --> 00:02:50.771
"That's okay." Julius shrugged.

46
00:02:50.772 --> 00:02:55.203
"The wrong person always gets accused first in spy stories."

47
00:02:55.204 --> 00:03:01.744
"Hmm," Ally said. "So how do investigators find the right person?"

48
00:03:01.745 --> 00:03:04.407
"They lay a trap," Julius said.

49
00:03:04.408 --> 00:03:09.161
"They get the suspect alone and try to get them to confess."

50
00:03:09.162 --> 00:03:11.861
"I know!" Ally said.

51
00:03:11.862 --> 00:03:18.039
"Let's ask Flo to come to Ray's house to taste your latest recipe idea, Barry.

52
00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:24.868
Then when we're all together, her heart will soften, and she'll confess everything."

53
00:03:24.869 --> 00:03:28.788
"It might work," Mateo said slowly.

54
00:03:28.789 --> 00:03:32.243
Barry shrugged. "It can't hurt."

55
00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:37.530
"Let's try it." Mateo pulled out his phone to text Flo.

56
00:03:37.531 --> 00:03:41.899
A few moments later, he saw a reply bubble on the screen.

57
00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:47.363
"She's writing back! Oh wait, the bubble went away."

58
00:03:47.364 --> 00:03:52.090
The bubble showed up and disappeared several more times.

59
00:03:52.091 --> 00:03:55.529
"This is kind of suspicious," Julius said.

60
00:03:55.530 --> 00:04:00.211
"She's probably crafting a careful reply to throw us off her trail."

61
00:04:00.212 --> 00:04:04.676
"Wait! She replied!" Mateo held his phone up:

62
00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:08.481
Sure. See you tomorrow night

63
00:04:08.482 --> 00:04:11.598
. "The trap is set," Ally

64
00:04:11.599 --> 00:04:16.010
said. "That's all well and good, but we have another problem," Barry

65
00:04:16.011 --> 00:04:20.894
said. "The stove is not working. We need it for the

66
00:04:20.895 --> 00:04:25.362
contest." "I'll text Papi and ask him who we should call," Mateo

67
00:04:25.363 --> 00:04:32.236
said. "Hopefully we can get it fixed

68
00:04:32.237 --> 00:04:37.321
quickly." "I don't get it," Ally said as she and Julius left the

69
00:04:37.322 --> 00:04:41.848
field. "Flo is our friend. It's one thing to tell Pepe's our

70
00:04:41.849 --> 00:04:45.481
recipes. But cutting power and fuel lines on the

71
00:04:45.482 --> 00:04:48.071
truck? That's a serious thing to do."

72
00:04:48.072 --> 00:04:51.800
"Maybe she didn't do it," Julius said.

73
00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:55.461
"Spies often have co-conspirators."

74
00:04:55.462 --> 00:05:00.778
Ally's jaw dropped. "You mean there's a whole gang of them?"

75
00:05:00.779 --> 00:05:03.287
"Could be," Julius said.

76
00:05:03.288 --> 00:05:06.725
"Guess you'll find out tomorrow night when she comes to your house."

77
00:05:06.726 --> 00:05:08.869
Ally sighed.

78
00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:14.261
She didn't like to think of Flo like this, as a spy, betraying her coworkers and friends.

79
00:05:14.262 --> 00:05:17.876
And what was Ray going to think about all this?

80
00:05:17.877 --> 00:05:21.292
"Hey, isn't that the show's producer and cameraperson?"

81
00:05:21.293 --> 00:05:26.451
Julius asked, pointing to two people leaving the field ahead of them.

82
00:05:26.452 --> 00:05:29.153
"What are they doing here?"

83
00:05:29.154 --> 00:05:36.347
Ally shrugged. "They film different locations around town to give viewers a sense of the place."

84
00:05:36.348 --> 00:05:40.271
"Right," Julius said.

85
00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:46.051
When they reached Ray's house, Ally and Julius agreed to make another date for the museum.

86
00:05:46.052 --> 00:05:50.230
"Oh, and text me after you meet with Flo," Julius said.

87
00:05:50.231 --> 00:05:54.670
"I will. Talk to you later!"

88
00:05:54.671 --> 00:05:57.674
Ally walked into the house.

89
00:05:57.675 --> 00:06:01.413
"I really hope we're wrong about Flo," she thought.

90
00:06:01.414 --> 00:06:05.160
"But I'm definitely not wrong about my powers.

91
00:06:05.161 --> 00:06:11.930
I hope Alpha's powers are working well now because she's the only one who can help me!"

